quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  2,146,"Those to whom We have given the Book recognise him (i.e. the Prophet Muhammad [blessings and peace be upon him]) as they recognise their sons. However, a group of them indeed conceals the truth while they know (very well)."
  2,147,"(This is) the truth from your Lord. So, do not be among those who doubt (the truth)."
  2,148,"Everyone has a direction towards which he turns. So take the lead in all good works. Wherever you may be, Allah will bring you all together. Indeed, Allah is All-Capable of everything."
  2,149,"So whichever path you set out on, turn your face towards the direction of the Sacred Mosque (at the time of prayer). And this is indeed the truth from your Lord. And Allah is not negligent of what you do."
  2,150,"So, whichever path you set out on, turn your face towards the direction of the Sacred Mosque (at the time of prayer). And wherever you may be (O Muslims), turn your faces towards it, so that the people may have no argument against you, except the wrongdoers among them. Do not fear them, but fear Me, so that I may complete My favour on you and so you may be (rightly) guided."
  2,151,"Thus, We have sent you a Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) from among yourselves, who recites Our revelations to you, purifies you, teaches you the Book and Wisdom and instructs you in (other) matters you did not know."
  2,152,"So remember Me; I will remember you. Be thankful to Me, and never be ungrateful to Me."
  2,153,"O believers! Seek help through patience and prayer. Indeed, Allah is with the patient."
